caption: End-of-Session Mark Procedure
rule: end-of-session-mark-procedure

Drive Marks are awarded once, at the end of each session.

Review every Drive currently listed on the character's Drive sheet.

For each Drive, decide whether the character meaningfully fulfilled it during the session.

Record one Drive Mark for each fulfilled Drive.

Do not award more than one Mark for the same Drive, regardless of how many times it was fulfilled during the session.

Use the honor system as the normal method: the player records clear awards without requiring individual GM approval.

When the player is uncertain or the application is disputed, ask the GM and use the GM's ruling.

The goal is consistent, low-friction reflection at the end of play. The procedure is not intended to require evidence logs, vote counting, or detailed accounting during the session.
